# ReplyComposer — the "post your reply" box under a post.
#
# ── WHY THE BUTTON IS IN THE SLOT ───────────────────────────────────────────
#
# ComposeBox owns its own button because the action it calls takes exactly one
# argument and that argument is its own cell: `post(draft)`. A reply cannot work
# that way. It calls `reply(id, draft)` — the post being replied to, and the text —
# and a component cannot make that call. An `action` reference parameter is
# invoked with no arguments (the rule forms/form.fct states, and the reason
# `SubmitButton` was removed from this library); a `text` parameter carrying the
# id would give the component the value but not the ability to name the action.
#
# So the component owns what is structural — the avatar column, the borderless
# input, the rule above the actions, the pending and error lines — and the caller
# writes the button in the slot, at the call site, WHERE THE ID IS IN SCOPE:
#
#     for t in Tweet where t.id == id by id desc limit 1:
#         use ReplyComposer("Post your reply", replyDraft):
#             button "Reply" -> reply(t.id, replyDraft)
#
# This is the same conclusion content/comments.fct reached for a comment's delete
# control, and it is worth stating twice: the shape of a reusable facet is decided
# by which of its calls carry arguments.
#
# ── THE CELL IS THE CALLER'S ────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# `v: cell text` rather than a `draft` this file names. A page with a composer at
# the top and a reply box under a post has two independent drafts, and a facet
# that hard-coded one cell would silently make them the same box: typing a reply
# would rewrite the post you were composing.
import "../ui/avatar.fct"
app FacetSocial:
    css:
        [data-fa-mount] .x-reply-c { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 40px minmax(0,1fr);
                      gap: 12px; padding: 12px 16px;
                      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--x-line, #2f3336); }
        [data-fa-mount] .x-reply-c input { border: none; background: none; font-size: 17px;
                            padding: 12px 0; width: 100%; color: var(--fa-fg); }
        [data-fa-mount] .x-reply-c input::placeholder { color: var(--fa-muted); }
        [data-fa-mount] .x-reply-actions { display: flex; justify-content: flex-end; align-items: center;
                            gap: 12px; border-top: 1px solid var(--x-line, #2f3336); padding-top: 12px; }
        [data-fa-mount] .x-reply-actions button { background: var(--fa-accent); color: #fff; font-weight: 700;
                                   padding: 8px 16px; border-radius: 9999px; }
    component ReplyComposer(placeholder: text, v: cell text):
        box class "x-reply-c":
            use Avatar(actor)
            box:
                input bind v placeholder "{placeholder}"
                row class "x-reply-actions":
                    slot
